						{
							"type": "paragraph",
							"attrs": {
								"dir": "auto"
							},
							"content": [
								{
									"type": "text",
									"text": "So far we discussed about pods, which deploy single instances of our application, such as the web application. In this case, each container is encapsulated in pods. Multiple such pods are deployed using replication controllers or replica sets. Then coms deployment, which is a Kubernetes object that comes higher in the hierarchy. The deployment provides us with the capcability to upgrade the underlying instances seamlessly using the rolling updates, undo changes, and pause and resume chnages as required"
								}
							]
						}
					]
				}
			},
