								"dir": "auto"
							},
							"content": [
								{
									"type": "text",
									"text": "Run the above command followed by the name of the deployment. The deployment will then destroy the pods in the replica set and bring the older ones up in the old replica set, and your application is back to its older format. when you compare the output of the cubecontrol, get replica sets command before and after the rollback. You will be able to notice this difference before the rollback. The first replica set had zero pods and new replica set had five pods, and this is reversed after the rollback is finished. To summarize the commands real quick, use the kubectl create command to create the deployment get deployments command to list the deployments. "
								}
							]
						}
					]
				}
