			"props": {
				"color": "black",
				"size": "s",
				"w": 1451.640625,
				"font": "draw",
				"textAlign": "start",
				"autoSize": false,
				"scale": 1,
				"richText": {
					"type": "doc",
					"attrs": {
						"dir": "auto"
					},
					"content": [
						{
							"type": "paragraph",
							"attrs": {
								"dir": "auto"
							},
							"content": [
								{
									"type": "text",
									"marks": [
										{
											"type": "code"
										}
									],
									"text": "Controller: "
								},
								{
									"type": "text",
									"text": "The controllers are the brain behind orchestration. They are responsible for noticing and ressponding when nodes, containers or endpoints goes down, the controllers make decisions to bring up new containers. In such cases, the container runtime is the underlying software that is used to run containers. In our case, it happens to be Docker, but there are other options as well"
								}
							]
						}
					]
				}
			},
			"parentId": "page:page",
			"index": "b1vMt2",
			"typeName": "shape"
		},
		{
			"x": 1036.7447388948171,
			"y": 16409.992399685347,
			"rotation": 0,
			"isLocked": false,
			"opacity": 1,
			"meta": {},
			"id": "shape:xz56p2N3ewEw2F34_4nb6",
			"type": "arrow",
			"props": {
				"kind": "arc",
				"elbowMidPoint": 0.5,
				"dash": "draw",
				"size": "s",
				"fill": "none",
