					"content": [
						{
							"type": "paragraph",
							"attrs": {
								"dir": "auto"
							},
							"content": [
								{
									"type": "text",
									"text": "Kubernetes uses YAML files as inputs for the creation of objects such as pods, replicas, deployments, Services, etc. all of these follow a similar structure. A Kubernetes definition file always contains four top level fields the API version, Kind, metadata, and Spec. These are top level or root level properties. These are also required fields, so you must have them in your configuration file."
								}
							]
						}
					]
				}
			},
