			"parentId": "page:f68luzkeSOzKLbQERhXxs",
			"index": "b6Q8MA",
			"typeName": "shape"
		},
		{
			"x": -6.601178788036123,
			"y": 12835.236715545725,
			"rotation": 0,
			"isLocked": false,
			"opacity": 1,
			"meta": {},
			"id": "shape:ZtLlUtldl6v8ksAgpqpDX",
			"type": "text",
			"props": {
				"color": "black",
				"size": "s",
				"w": 1462.98828125,
				"font": "draw",
				"textAlign": "start",
				"autoSize": false,
				"scale": 1,
				"richText": {
					"type": "doc",
					"attrs": {
						"dir": "auto"
					},
					"content": [
						{
							"type": "paragraph",
							"attrs": {
								"dir": "auto"
							},
							"content": [
								{
									"type": "text",
									"text": "Suppose for example, you have a web server that needs to be deployed in a production environment. you might need multiple instances, for obvious reasons Secondly, whenever newer versions of applicaiton builds become available on the docker registry, you would like to upgrade your docker instances seamlessly. However, when you upgrade your instances, you do not want to upgrade all of them at once. This may impact users accessing our applications, so you might want to upgrade them one after the other. And that kind of upgrade is known as rolling updated. Suppose one of the upgrades you performed resulted in an unexpected error, and you’re asked to undo the recent change you would like to be able to roll back the changes that were recently carried out. Finally, say for example, you would like to make multiple changes to your environment, such as upgrading the underlying web server versions, as well as scaling your envrionment and also modifying the resource allocations, etc, you do not want to apply each change immediately after the command is run. Instead, you would like to apply a path to your environment, make the changes and then resume so that all the changes are rolled out together. All of these capabilities are available with the kubernetes deployments."
								}
							]
						}
					]
				}
			},
			"parentId": "page:f68luzkeSOzKLbQERhXxs",
